---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Show which instrumented code of a run it reached, as a tree of modules, files,
classes and functions. Use it to find code that the run never reached, and the
moment where it first reached a location. Runs created before release 67.6 have
no coverage.

`runs coverage` is an unstable feature: its flags and output can change in any
release. Enable it with `SNOUTY_UNSTABLE_FEATURES=coverage`.

Each line starts with COVERAGE: the share of the instrumented locations under it
that the run reached, then the reached and total counts in SI notation, such as
`66.7%  2/3` or `28.7%  1.1k/4k`. 0% is yellow, and 100% green. Then comes the
node, under its parent: a module with its ID, name and language; its files,
sorted by path; and with --rollup `function` or `none`, the classes or types of
each file, then their functions, both in source order.

A class is the API's class of a function: a Java or C# class, a Go method's
receiver type or a Python class. For native code, it is the type of a demangled
`<Type>::method`, and a `<Type as Trait>::method` shows as `Trait::method`. Free
functions come first, under `(no class)`, and a file of free functions only has
no class level.

--rollup sets the deepest level: `file` (the default), `function`, or `none` for
every location. With `none`, a table of the function's locations hangs under
each function, in source order: START and END of the span, as line:column, then
INPUT_HASH and VTIME, the moment where the run first reached it. Pass them as
the input_hash and vtime of `runs logs` to read the logs up to that moment. A
reached location is plain, an unreached one dim, and an empty cell is `-`.
Several locations can share a span, such as the copies of a generic function, or
the two outcomes of a branch; each is its own row.

The filters keep only some of the coverage. --module takes a module ID, which
`runs modules` lists. --module-name takes a glob over the module's name, --file
over the file's path, --class over the class's full or short name, and
--function over the function's name. A file glob without a `/` matches the
file's base name, and in a path `*` stays within a directory and `**` crosses
them. A filter's values are alternatives, and the filters together narrow the
output: --file `api.go` --file `raft.go` --class `Raft` keeps Raft's methods in
either file. A value with a leading `!` excludes what it matches instead, such
as `!**/vendor/**`; quote it in the shell. `\!` starts a value with a literal
`!`. The server applies --module and --module-name, and snouty applies the rest
while the locations download.

VTIME is cut to five decimals, which still names a moment at or before the first
reach. With --detail, it prints whole. On a terminal, file names are shortened
at the start, and other names at the end. After the output, a status line on
stderr counts the locations, and gives the share reached and the run's status.

With --json, each module prints as one JSON object on its own line, nested like
the text down to --rollup: the module's `module_id`, `module_name`, `language`,
`reached` and `total`, then `files`, each with its `classes`, each with its
`functions`. A class is its full name, or null for free functions. A function
has the `first_reached` moment of its earliest location, and with `none` its
`locations`, as the API sends them, with each vtime as a JSON number. The counts
are exact.

While the run is in progress, the output is the coverage up to now. The run must
be ready or complete. If it is not, the command waits until it is ready, and
says that it waits.

Examples:
  snouty runs coverage <run_id>
  snouty runs coverage <run_id> --rollup function --file '!**/vendor/**'
  snouty runs coverage <run_id> --rollup none --module <module_id> --class Raft

Usage: snouty runs coverage [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID>

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>
          Run ID

Options:
      --module <MODULE_ID>
          Only the module with this ID (repeatable; a leading ! excludes it)

      --module-name <GLOB>
          Only modules whose name matches this glob (repeatable; a leading !
          excludes them)

      --file <GLOB>
          Only files whose path matches this glob (repeatable; a leading !
          excludes them)

      --class <GLOB>
          Only classes or types whose name matches this glob (repeatable; a
          leading ! excludes them)

      --function <GLOB>
          Only functions whose name matches this glob (repeatable; a leading !
          excludes them)

      --rollup <ROLLUP>
          The deepest level of the tree: files, functions, or every location

          Possible values:
          - file:     Modules and their files
          - function: Modules, files, classes and functions
          - none:     Modules, files, classes, functions and every location
          
          [default: file]

  -d, --detail
          Print each vtime whole

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Print NDJSON: one JSON object per line

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
